  "compatibility_findings": [
    "Current official complete compatibility table requires A3/HCCS device_sdma: LingQu L1 >=1.5.0 (prefers 1.5.1), HDK >=25.5.1, firmware >=7.8.0.6.201 and OS kernel >=5.10.0; BIOS guidance depends on memory capacity.",
    "MemFabric v1.2.0 README requires CANN >=8.1.RC1, GLIBC >=2.28, DRAM pooling HDK >=25.5.0 (recommends25.5.1), LingQu1.5.0 and matching1520L1 update. Current table is stricter for HDK; observed25.5.2 exceeds both numeric lower bounds.",
    "Existing evidence has HDK25.5.2, CANN9.1.0 and a firmware sample7.8.0.7.220. LingQu L1 version remains unverified. A sample is not all-device firmware validation.",
    "v1.2.0 configuration supports explicit device_sdma and 1GiB DRAM/HBM alignment. Python API documents close(); no special close ordering found in the reviewed installation/API pages that explains the observed heap corruption."
  ],
  "abi_lead": {
    "official_issue": "https://gitcode.com/Ascend/memcache/issues/281",
    "official_merge_request": "https://gitcode.com/Ascend/memcache/merge_requests/536",
    "retrievable_official_merge_description": "https://gitcode.com/Ascend/memcache/tree/develop/script",
    "description": "Official upstream describes MetaService coredump caused by C++/STL symbol interposition when build-time and runtime MemFabric minor version or C++ ABI differ; change uses C ABI wrappers, version/symbol checks and RTLD_LOCAL|RTLD_DEEPBIND.",
    "source_verification": "The installed MemCache v1.2.0 source directly links smem_shared and acc_tcp_net_static and has no smem_get_abi_version or RTLD_DEEPBIND checks. Reviewed release/1.2 tip1.2.1 also lacks that isolation; reviewed master1.5.0 contains it. The merge description names develop1.3 at its own merge time; do not treat that as current master version.",
    "limits": "Observed local failure is post-close heap corruption, while upstream description discusses startup C++ string-copy coredumps. Runtime ELF/library paths, symbol bindings, build ABI flags and native crash stack have not been collected. This is a related diagnosis lead, not a confirmed cause or verified fix for this environment."
  },
